    description: "From WI-borib (docs/audits/0026). Verdict RENAME (different questions, unnamed in the output) plus one projection defect.\n\n1. \"The important symbols\" is answered by three populations: symbols ranks every node (externals and stand-ins included, 5 of 14 rows on agent B's fixture); sketch Key Symbols ranks the KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS allowlist; compact's default ranks any kind as a bridge with key-only seeds (by design, fa7ae4e388). WI-zulij aligned the population and test-edge filter (5e4fbcf7a4) and recorded 55% top-10 agreement; nothing pins agreement end to end. None of the outputs says which population it ranks.\n2. A compact output's metrics.languages counts the COMPACTED subset under the field name the survey uses for the whole repo (ripgrep: survey rust 5,163 nodes / 97 files, compact 100 / 2).\n3. DEFECT: compact's node projection drops discovery_language, so a route/stand-in node whose language lives only there counts as language unknown -- reproduced on real output, mitmproxy compact metrics.languages carries unknown: {nodes: 1} (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/borib_consumer_agreement_10302026/M/b/).\n\nACCEPTANCE: each view's output names the population it ranks or counts; compact's projection keeps discovery_language."  # a7d3
    fields: {}  # a7d3
